A||||11||mrfixit58||Front License Plate Bracket Removal||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-10-2000||02:29 PM||||Well, my new (used) 87 GT should be here today. I bought it from someone in one of those states that require a front license plate. Since Florida doesn't, I would like to remove it. Am I going to have holes in the front facia? If so, has anyone been sucessful in patching then and repainting?<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy||||reg||5
Z||000001||lennyb4||07-10-2000||02:32 PM||||Yep..your gonna have holes there. And you should be able to fill them quite easily. Try a paintable epoxy mixture. Im not to sure on how good standard filler would hold up due to the amout of flex placed on the facia's.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||07-10-2000||02:32 PM||||No holes.  You'll need about a 8" extension for your socket.  With the plate off, look into the holder.  You'll see the bolts.  They just screw into a couple of pieces of plastic.  Unscrew them and pull it off.  Mine rubbed the paint off of the fascia some, but no big deal.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||07-10-2000||02:54 PM||||Hummmm... Conflicting opinions...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Sounds like it may depend on "who" actually installed the bracket.<P>Roy||||reg||4
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||07-10-2000||03:14 PM||||If its the factory plate holder NO, NO HOLES!!||||reg||14
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||07-10-2000||03:26 PM||||ON<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=15436465&Sequence=2"> <P>OFF<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723601&p=18365627&Sequence=2"> <P>just for shows, here in cali. you gotta have a front plate!!!! <p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 07-10-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000006||mrfixit58||07-10-2000||03:46 PM||||Well, the car is FROM California. Was bought and driven there it's whole life. My guess is that it's factory. <P>Still waiting on the inept shipping company to call... again. I gave them three numbers to reach me. So, what does the trucker do? he leaves me a message on my home recorder and says "I need directions to your house" and doesn't leave a phone number so I can return his call.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> And, of course, their customer service is NO help... How do these people stay in business???... surely not by repeat business! <P>I WANT MY CAR!!!!<P>Sorry... just venting,<BR>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bugsy||07-10-2000||04:04 PM||||hey DXR...did my eyes detect some driving lights mounted in that nose?...how did you mount them? TIA<BR>Kevin||||reg||14
Z||000008||DXR_DAD||07-10-2000||05:04 PM||||Yes Bugsy!!! They are mounted to the steel frame just behind the facsia, with L brackets. the holes are already in the frame<BR>to mount the brackets  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DXR_DAD||||reg||12
Z||000009||hugh||07-10-2000||08:04 PM||||Roy,I bought my car in Louisiana.It was supposed to be picked up by May 15 and brought to New Jersey in about 5-7 days.I called them on the 16th. and that's when they started trying to get the car picked up.I got the car around June 3rd.I paid $1300.00 up front for an enclosed carrier.I used AAAdvantage in Phoenix. ||||reg||1
